Milestone 2 Analytical Report
ClimateScope – Milestone 2: Core Analysis & Visualization Design
1. Objective

Milestone 2 focused on:

Performing statistical and seasonal analysis

Identifying extreme weather events

Comparing regional climate behavior

Selecting effective visualization techniques

Designing the conceptual layout of an interactive dashboard

2. Statistical Analysis

Descriptive statistics were computed for:

Temperature

Humidity

Wind speed

Precipitation

Key observations:

Temperature values showed moderate spread across regions

Precipitation distribution was right-skewed, indicating occasional heavy rainfall

Humidity exhibited regional clustering patterns

Correlation heatmaps revealed relationships such as:

Temperature and humidity showing weak-to-moderate correlation

Wind speed largely independent from precipitation

3. Seasonal Patterns and Trends

Monthly aggregation highlighted clear seasonal cycles:

Temperature peaks during summer months

Rainfall increases during monsoon or wet seasons

Humidity trends follow rainfall intensity in many regions

Seasonal variation differed significantly across countries, confirming strong geographical climate diversity.

4. Extreme Weather Events

Extreme temperature events were detected using:

1st percentile (extreme low)

99th percentile (extreme high)

Findings:

Certain years recorded noticeably higher extreme-event counts

A small subset of countries contributed disproportionately to extremes

Extreme events displayed temporal clustering rather than uniform distribution

These insights are critical for climate risk awareness and monitoring.

5. Regional Weather Comparison

Country-level aggregation produced:

Average temperature per country

Total precipitation per country

Mean humidity per country

Comparative analysis showed:

Clear separation between hot and cool regions

Significant rainfall imbalance across countries

Humidity patterns aligned with precipitation zones

This confirms strong regional climate variability.

6. Visualization Design Choices

The following visualizations were selected for clarity and interpretability:

Histograms → variable distributions

Correlation heatmaps → inter-variable relationships

Line charts → seasonal and temporal trends

Scatter plots → extreme event behavior

Bar charts → regional comparisons

Boxplots → distribution differences across countries

These collectively support multi-level climate insight exploration.

7. Dashboard Wireframe Concept

The proposed interactive dashboard layout:

Top Section

Title and global filters (Year, Country, Month)

Middle Section

Line charts for temperature and rainfall trends

Bottom Section

Correlation heatmap

Regional comparison bar charts

Extreme-event visualizations

This structure ensures:

Logical information flow

Clear comparison across regions and time

User-friendly analytical exploration

8. Milestone 2 Conclusion

Milestone 2 successfully delivered:

Comprehensive statistical understanding

Detection and analysis of extreme weather events

Regional climate comparison insights

Well-justified visualization strategy

A structured dashboard design blueprint

This completes the core analytical foundation required for building the final interactive ClimateScope dashboard in the next milestone.